raltbos@xs4all.nl (Richard Bos) wrote:
> Patric Mueller <bhaak@bigfoot.com> wrote:
>
>> I don't know how much the DevTeam wants to follow the mythology.
>
> Not very closely.

In that case: NHINGM (NetHack Is Not Greek Mythology). :-)

>> After all Perseus wasn't stoned so how can there be his statue.
>> Perseus used his shield to view Medusa as her reflected gaze has
>> apparently lost its stoning property so how can she be stoned by her
>> own gaze with a mirror?
>
> Now you're mixing two versions of the story, as well.
>
> In NetHack, Medusa's attack is a gaze attack, 

Mostly.

If you are polymorphed into a monster with a gaze attack, you can also
be stoned by gazing at her.

The source code comment explains this as follows:
 /* Technically this one shouldn't affect you at all because
  * the Medusa gaze is an active monster attack that only
  * works on the monster's turn, but for it to *not* have an
  * effect would be too weird.

> a dead Medusa is as
> innocuous as a stoned one (as long as you don't try to eat her), and

Dying from looking at her dead body would fit nicely into NetHack.

> Medusa herself is resistant to any kind of stoning except from her own
> reflected attack, which is the most likely way for her to die.

> In Greek mythology, Medusa's stoning was an effect of _you_ looking on
> _her_, which continued to work after her death, her own gaze did nothing
> to her whether reflected or not,

As Perseus himself didn't turned to stone when looking at her
reflected image I wonder if this was only because he didn't use a
perfectly reflecting mirror but only a polished shield that must have
distorted her ugly look.

> and she died because Perseus ran her through with his sword.

After which Pegasus and Chryasor sprang from her head.

Slash'Em at least features Pegasus.

> IOW, the NetHack Medusa is about as close to the myth as most "based on
> a real story" TV films are to the original real story.

Well, this is not the first case of "Adaption Decay" in NetHack. :)

But didn't the original programmer know any better or did he just try
to make her fit into NetHacks attack framework?

